  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Interfaces and requests",
      "items": [
        "The agent uses stdio; the MCP service connects to the running Blender TCP bridge.",
        "The TCP bridge defaults to localhost:9876; arrows distinguish requests and returned results."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Who controls the service?",
      "items": [
        "The client launches and manages the independent MCP service via command; the TCP bridge is started inside Blender.",
        "Blender's bridge controls operate the bridge, not the client's stdio process."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Installation locations and processes",
      "items": [
        "Background frames mark installation areas; node subtitles identify processes. One package may supply code for separate processes.",
        "Tools and dependencies live in the uv environment; the Extension lives in Blender's user repository. They are installed separately."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Local configuration",
      "items": [
        "The client and Blender run in the same native OS on one computer; use the actual configured ports and paths.",
        "The client stores the MCP command and bridge host / port; uv tool dir reports the actual tool directory."
      ]
    }
  ]
